 This instruction gives a brief overview on how to use the provided (and recommended) tools to perform the cross-checking of the LCEVC conformance test bitstreams.\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAACGJ}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAACGJ}
{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Test Scripts
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Test Scripts}
The {\i cross_checking_tools}  folder on the MPEG FTP server contains the following content:{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b stresstest.py} - The python script to perform the tests with\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
tests.json - A json file which contains the settings for the individual tests\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
