{{\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Performing a Test
\par}
{\tc\tcl2 \v Performing a Test}
Most of the tests can be run automatically without any additional input. The python script {\b stresstest.py} can be used to perform the encodes and decodes. Additionally, the reconstruction yuv file of the encoder and the yuv of the decoder are checked whether they are matching. In case, multiple cores are available to perform the tests, the following command lines can be appended by the argument {
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid --parallel=10\par
}
 where the number of parallel jobs can be specified.\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAACGM}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAACGM}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
H.264/AVC Base Codec
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v H.264/AVC Base Codec}
The following command line gives an example for running the python script on the Cactus sequence: {
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid python stresstest.py \par
--progress=spinner \par
--encoder=lcevc_test_model/ModelEncoder \par
--decoder=lcevc_test_model/ModelDecoder \par
--label="Cactus_" \par
--test_file=tests.json \par
--parameters='\{\\"input_file\\":\\"input_yuvs/Cactus_49frames_1920x1080_50fps_420.yuv\\",\\"format\\":\\"yuv420p\\",\\"base_encoder\\":\\"avc\\"\}' \par
--sets="stress"\par
}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAACGN}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAACGN}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
H.265/HEVC Base Codec
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v H.265/HEVC Base Codec}
The following command line gives an example for running the python script on the ParkRunning3 sequence: {
\par
\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid python stresstest.py \par
--progress=spinner \par
--encoder=lcevc_test_model/ModelEncoder \par
--decoder=lcevc_test_model/ModelDecoder \par
--label="ParkRunning3_" \par
--test_file=tests.json \par
--parameters='\{\\"input_file\\":\\"input_yuvs/ParkRunning3_63frames_3840x2160_50fps_10bit_420.yuv\\",\\"format\\":\\"yuv420p10\\",\\"base_encoder\\":\\"hevc\\"\}' \par
--sets="stress,stress_10bit"\par
}
\par}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAACGO}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAACGO}
{{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid 
Special Tests
\par}
{\tc\tcl3 \v Special Tests}
Some tests cannot be performed automatically and need manual input.\par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
For Cactus & CanYouReadThis, the tests "RBD-1" and "RBD-2" require as an input the 10 bit yuv file (provided in the folder inputs_yuv). Additionally, the format needs to be changed to "yuv420p10". These tests can be run by specifying {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid --sets="stress_10bit"\par
}
 on the command line of the python script.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
The tests "RBD-3 and RBD-4" require as an input the 12 bit yuv file (provided in the folder inputs_yuv). Additionally, the format needs to be changed to "yuv420p12". These tests can be run by specifying {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid --sets="stress_12bit"\par
}
 on the command line of the python script.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
The test "CST-1" require as an input a monochrome yuv file (4:0:0) (provided in the folder inputs_yuv). Additionally, the format needs to be changed to "y" for Cactus & CanYouReadThis and to "y10" for ParkRunning3. The test can be run by specifying {
\par
\pard\plain \s41\li360\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid --sets="stress_mono"\par
}
 on the command line of the python script.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
For the tests "HDUD-1" through "HDUD-4", the user data must be extracted. This can be done by compiling the LCEVC Test Model (LTM) with "USER_DATA_EXTRACTION" (located in {\b src/Config.hpp}) turned on. The user data from the encoder and decoder will be written into a binary file. These files can be cross-checked with the files provided on the MPEG FTP server.\par}
\par
\par}
\par}
